*.h linguist-detectable=false
*.c linguist-detectable=false

# Golden sing-box configs are compared with bytes.Equal against output the test
# generates with LF. core.autocrlf=true on a Windows build machine checks them
# out as CRLF, so every golden assertion would fail on a fresh clone while
# passing for whoever generated them. Pin to LF.
v2/config/testdata/golden/*.json text eol=lf

# Deliberately NOT `*.go text eol=lf`. Some upstream Go files are stored CRLF,
# which inflates their diffs ~40x -- v2/hcore/grpc_server.go reports 296/300 but
# is 3/7 under --ignore-cr-at-eol -- and makes cherry-picks conflict on whole
# files. Pinning *.go would not fix those blobs now; it would defer a whole-file
# rewrite to whenever someone next edits one, landing a 300-line phantom diff in
# an unrelated commit. merge.renormalize=true handles the cherry-pick side
# without touching the index. See docs/upstream/METHODOLOGY.md in the app repo.
